# windows.storage: Add StorageFile with GetFileFromPathAsync() and the basic IStorageItem properties.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12734 state=closed
# Wine has no Windows.Storage.StorageFile class; IStorageFileStatics is only forward-declared. Apps that get a path from a file picker and turn it into a StorageFile therefore fail at activation. Minecraft Bedrock's "Import world" is one of them: after the picker returns, it calls StorageFile.GetFileFromPathAsync() on the chosen path and then reads the item's Path and Name.

This MR adds the class in C to windows.storage:

- The IDL gets IStorageFileStatics and the types its signatures need, and StorageFile is declared with its statics and as agile.
- Tests come first, with todo_wine that the later commits remove.
- A runtimeclass stub registers StorageFile and returns the statics.
- GetFileFromPathAsync() runs on the thread pool like the other async operations here, using an IAsyncOperation\<IInspectable \*\> helper taken from windows.devices.radios. An empty or relative path fails with E_INVALIDARG, a missing file with the Win32 error, and a directory with ERROR_DIRECTORY.
- Name, Path, Attributes, DateCreated and IsOfType() on IStorageItem, and FileType and ContentType on IStorageFile. Everything else stays a FIXME stub.

The error codes for relative, empty and directory paths, and returning an empty ContentType when the extension has no "Content Type" value, were picked without checking on Windows. E_INVALIDARG for a relative path matches the "Value does not fall within the expected range" error .NET reports in that case.

I tested on macOS with both 64-bit and 32-bit (wow64) builds. The windows.storage tests pass at every commit with no skips. On the final tree, windows.storage.applicationdata, windows.applicationmodel, ole32 compobj/marshal and combase roapi/string pass too. I also broke the code on purpose ten ways (wrong error for a NULL out pointer, no relative-path or directory check, wrong error for a missing file, wrong Name, Path, IsOfType, Attributes, DateCreated and ContentType), and the tests caught each one.

I also ran Minecraft Bedrock with this ser
